      "prompt": "Edit the supplied source photograph into Torn Washi Scene Collage / 和纸胶带场景拼贴. Produce one complete portrait 3:4 image, at least 1086 by 1448 pixels.\nObserved source: 芥末黄色小屋正面有三角白檐、左侧深绿玻璃格门、右侧白框窗；右下方银色单车及两车轮完整，左下有陶盆绿植，后方蓝海与白云，房屋面板和阴影自然，无招牌文字。\nMedium: An entire scene assembled from matte torn washi tape, where overlapping strips and fibers replace photographic surfaces.\nRebuild the full supplied scene as one portrait 3:4 handmade tape picture, keeping the kiosk and bicycle as its clear focus.\nConstruct every pictorial surface from torn washi or masking-tape pieces; do not leave an intact photographic layer beneath decorative strips.\nSample mustard yellow, deep green, sea blue and cloud white from the photograph, using matte paper versions of those colors.\nShow uneven torn ends, delicate fibers and slight translucency; overlapped tape creates subtle darker color intersections.\nAlign long strips with walls, roof edges and the horizon; use smaller torn pieces for foliage, clouds and bicycle structure.\nKeep door, window, wheels, frame and plant placement identifiable; simplify spokes without merging or breaking the bicycle’s connections.\nUse shallow contact shadows between paper layers only; preserve an overall flat handmade picture rather than a deep sculptural diorama.\nLet outer tape edges end naturally on clean white backing; add no typography, brand marks, exterior frame or watermark.\nPreserve: Retain the source building silhouette, roof, openings, bicycle placement and plant relationships. Keep relative proportions and viewpoint while replacing texture with tape; tiny details may simplify but structural joints remain connected. Use source-derived scene elements only; decorative tape is a material, not permission to invent new objects.\nAvoid: A photograph merely bordered with tape, painted watercolor pretending to be tape, smooth vector shapes or glossy plastic strips. Disconnected bicycle, missing openings, invented signs, heavy embossing, deep diorama shadows, cluttered craft table or watermark.\nReturn only the finished image.",
